<title>USA: USDA boosts export credits to Russia by $25 Mln.</title>
<headline>USDA boosts export credits to Russia by $25 Mln.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Department said Monday it increased to $95 million its offer of export credit guarantees to assist sales of farm goods to Russia during fiscal 1997.</p>
<p>Previously, USDA had offered $70 million in credits.</p>
<p>USDA said all other terms and conditions were unchanged.</p>
<p>The short-term credits were offered to the private sector.</p>
</text>
